<FeaturesPage
  title="Midweek Mashers — Noah Lee"
  description="How I grew the Melty Blood scene from a small community to 200+ players at majors — through event series, format design, and tools built for organizers."
  eyebrow="Community / FGC"
  headline="Midweek Mashers"
  headlineEmphasis="Online Event Community"
  items={midweekMashers}
  backHref="/work"
  backLabel="All work"
>
  <p slot="lede">
    Niche games tend to have fragmented communities and scattered events: join a new Discord server for every tournament, and hope you catch event announcements in time. I build Midweek Mashers as a hub for MBAACC and FPAN online events. It's the original hub for Adomin and built to onboard other organizers in the scene to run their own events to centralize more events in one place.
  </p>
  <p class="contact__lede" slot="outro">
    Playing Melty Blood, developing a community, or want to talk about running events? <a href="https://x.com/enpicie" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em class="serif-italic">Find me on X</em></a>.
  </p>
</FeaturesPage>
